{"body": "Resolution Number TMBC206-03-23 of the Duly Elected and Certified Governing Body of the Turtle Mountain Band of Chippewa Indians WHEREAS, the Turtle Mountain Band of Chippewa Indians, hereinafter referred to as the Tribe, is an unincorporated Band acting under a revised Constitution and By-Laws approved by the Secretary of the Interior on June 16 th , 1959, and amendments thereto approved; and WHEREAS, Article IX (a) Section 1 of the Turtle Mountain Constitution and By-Laws empowers the Tribal Council with the authority to represent the Band and to negotiate with the Federal, State and Local governments and with private persons; and WHEREAS, Article IX (a) Section 1 of the Turtle Mountain Constitution and Bylaws requires a 30-day comment period prior to the adoption of any ordinances or amendments to the Tribal Code, whether proposed by resolution or otherwise. Adoption must occur through a roll call vote of the Tribal Council at a publicly held meeting; and WHEREAS, the Tribe proposes amendments to Title 25 , Section 25.0213 (Gaming Code) striking number 8c which states: \"Play in tournaments when the casino contributes prize money\"; now THEREFORE BE IT RESOLVED that the Tribe is approving a 30-day public comment period for proposed amendments to Title 25 , Section 25.0213 striking number 8c which states: \"Play in tournaments when the casino contributes prize money\" of the Tribal Gaming Code. CERTIFICATION I, the undersigned Tribal Secretary of the Turtle Mountain Band of Chippewa Indians, do hereby certify that the Tribal Council is composed of nine (9) members of whom nine (9) constituting a quorum were present at a meeting duly called, convened and held on the 21 st day of March, 2023 that the foregoing resolution was adopted by an affirmative vote of eight (8) in favor \u2013 Representatives Craig Lunday, Chad Counts, Elmer Davis Jr., Blaine \"Slugger\" Davis, Lynn Gourneau, Ron Trottier Sr., Jon Jon Keplin and Kenneth Malaterre; none (0) opposed; none (0) absent; with the Tribal Chairman not voting. _____________________________ Jolean A. Morin, Tribal Secretary ( ) SIGNED INTO LAW/Dated this____day of _____________, 2023 ( ) VETOED/Dated this_____day of ______________, 2023 _____________________________ Jamie Azure, Tribal Chairman", "num": "206-03-23", "path": "library|us/nsn/tmchippewa/council/resolutions|2023|Turtle Mountain Band of Chippewa Indians Res. No. 206-03-23", "title": "Resolution Number TMBC206-03-23 of the Duly Elected and Certified Governing Body of the Turtle Mountain Band of Chippewa Indians", "url": "/us/nsn/tmchippewa/council/resolutions/2023/206-03-23"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/tmchippewa/council/resolutions/2023/113-02-23", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Resolution Number TMBC113-02-23 of the Duly Elected and Certified Governing Body of the Turtle Mountain Band of Chippewa Indians WHEREAS, the Turtle Mountain Band of Chippewa Indians, hereinafter referred to as the Tribe, is an unincorporated Band acting under a revised Constitution and By-Laws approved by the Secretary of the Interior on June 16 th , 1959 and amendments thereto approved; and WHEREAS, Article IX(a) Section 1 of the Turtle Mountain Constitution and By-Laws empowers the Tribal Council with the authority to represent the Band and to negotiate with Federal, State, and Local Governments and with private persons; and WHEREAS, Article IX(a) Section 1 of the Turtle Mountain Constitution and By-Laws requires a 30-day comment period prior to the adoption of any ordinances or amendments to the Tribal Code, whether proposed by resolution or otherwise. Adoption must occur through a roll call vote of the Tribal Council at a publicly held meeting; and WHEREAS, the Tribe proposes revisions to Title 43 to provide for changes to the Lending Title to provide better protection for the tribe and the borrowers; and no THEREFORE BE IT RESOLVED that the Tribe is approving a 30 day public comment period for proposed revisions to Title 43 of the Credit Transaction Code. CERTIFICATION I, the undersigned Tribal Secretary of the Turtle Mountain Band of Chippewa Indians, do hereby certify that the Tribal Council is composed of nine (9) members of whom seven (7) constituting a quorum were present at a meeting duly called, convened and held on the 7 th day of February, 2023, that the foregoing resolution was adopted by an affirmative vote of all six (6) in favor -Reps. Lynn Gourneau, Ron Trottier, Kenneth Malaterre, Craig Lunday, Jon Jon Keplin, and Chad Counts; one (1) absent- Rep. Blaine \u201cSlugger\u201d Davis none (0) opposed; with the Vice-Chairman not voting. __________________________ Jolean A. Morin, Tribal Secretary ( ) SIGNED INTO LAW/Dated this ___ day of ___________, 2023 ( ) VETOED/Dated this ____ day of ______________, 2023 __________________________ Elmer Davis Jr., Vice-Chairman Jamie Azure, Tribal Chairman", "num": "113-02-23", "path": "library|us/nsn/tmchippewa/council/resolutions|2023|Turtle Mountain Band of Chippewa Indians Res. No. 113-02-23", "title": "Resolution Number TMBC113-02-23 of the Duly Elected and Certified Governing Body of the Turtle Mountain Band of Chippewa Indians", "url": "/us/nsn/tmchippewa/council/resolutions/2023/113-02-23"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/tmchippewa/council/resolutions/2022/14-12-22", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Resolution Number TMBC14-12-22 of the Duly Elected and Certified Governing Body of the Turtle Mountain Band of Chippewa Indians WHEREAS, the Turtle Mountain Band of Chippewa Indians, hereinafter referred to as the Tribe, is an unincorporated Band acting under a revised Constitution and By-Laws approved by the Secretary of the Interior on June 16 th , 1959 and amendments thereto approved; and WHEREAS, Article IX (a) Section 1 of the Turtle Mountain Constitution and By-Laws empowers the Tribal Council with the authority to represent the Band and to negotiate with Federal, State, and Local Governments and with private persons; and WHEREAS, Article IX (a) Section 1 of the Turtle Mountain Constitution and Bylaws requires a 30-day comment period prior to the adoption of any ordinances or amendments to the Tribal Code, whether proposed by resolution or otherwise. Adoption must occur through a roll call vote of the Tribal Council at a publicly held meeting; and WHEREAS, the Tribe adopted the Law Enforcement Act of 2017 (Chapter 50.06) by Resolution No. TMBC448-08-17, to provide for public safety through proactive and responsive law enforcement services; and WHEREAS, the Tribe is amending Title 50, Chapter 50.06 Section 50.0615 to add the attached proposed amendments to Section 50.0615 of the Law Enforcement Act of 2017 and amend the title of Chapter 50.06 to DIVISION OF LAW ENFORCEMENT-THE LAW ENFORCEMENT ACT OF 2017; and WHEREAS, the Tribe, by Resolution No. TMBC1970-11-12, is approved a comment period for proposed amendments to the Law Enforcement Act of 2017 by adding to Title 50, Chapter 50.06 Section 50.0615 the attached proposed amendments and amend the title of Chapter 50.06 to DIVISION OF LAW ENFORCEMENT-THE LAW ENFORCEMENT ACT OF 2017 to provide for public safety through proactive and responsive law enforcement services; and to educate and serve the public and no comments were received; now THEREFORE BE IT RESOLVED that the Tribe is approving the amendments to Title 50 as presented and will codify the Tribal Code accordingly. CERTIFICATION I, the undersigned, Tribal Secretary of the Turtle Mountain Band of Chippewa Indians, do hereby certify that the Tribal Council is composed of nine (9) members of whom eight (8) constituting a quorum were present at a meeting duly called, convened and held on the 22 nd day of December, 2022 that the foregoing resolution was adopted by an affirmative vote of seven (7) in favor - Representative Ron Trottier, Sr., Jon Jon Keplin, Lynn Gourneau, Craig Lunday, Kenneth Malaterre, Elmer Davis, Jr. and Chad Counts, one (1) absent- Reps. Blaine \"Slugger\" Davis; none (0) opposed; none (0) absent; with the Tribal Chairman not voting. ___________________________________ Jolean A. Morin, Tribal Secretary ( ) SIGNED INTO LAW/Dated this ___ day of __________, 2022 ( ) VETOED/Dated this ___ day of __________, 2022 ___________________________________ Jamie Azure, Tribal Chairman", "num": "14-12-22", "path": "library|us/nsn/tmchippewa/council/resolutions|2022|Turtle Mountain Band of Chippewa Indians Res. No. 14-12-22", "title": "Resolution Number TMBC14-12-22 of the Duly Elected and Certified Governing Body of the Turtle Mountain Band of Chippewa Indians", "url": "/us/nsn/tmchippewa/council/resolutions/2022/14-12-22"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/tmchippewa/council/resolutions/2022/1913-10-22", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Resolution Number TMBC1913-10-22 of the Duly Elected and Certified Governing Body of the Turtle Mountain Band of Chippewa Indians WHEREAS, the Turtle Mountain Band of Chippewa Indians, hereinafter referred to as the Tribe, is an unincorporated Band acting under a revised Constitution and By-Laws approved by the Secretary of the Interior on June 16 th , 1959 and amendments thereto approved; and WHEREAS, Article IX (a) Section 1 of the Turtle Mountain Constitution and By-Laws empowers the Tribal Council with the authority to represent the Band and to negotiate with Federal, State, and Local Governments and with private persons; and WHEREAS, Article IX (a) Section 1 of the Turtle Mountain Constitution and Bylaws requires a 30-day comment period prior to the adoption of any ordinances or amendments to the Tribal Code, whether proposed by resolution or otherwise. Adoption must occur through a roll call vote of the Tribal Council at a publicly held meeting; and WHEREAS, Title 52, the Tribal Health Emergencies Code was out for 30-day public comment with no issues on the proposed amendment to Title 52; now THEREFORE BE IT RESOLVED that the Tribe is approving proposed amendments to Title 52 of the Tribal Health Emergencies Code. CERTIFICATION I, the undersigned, Tribal Secretary of the Turtle Mountain Band of Chippewa Indians, do hereby certify that the Tribal Council is composed of nine (9) members of whom nine (9) constituting a quorum were present at a meeting duly called, convened and held on the 6 th day of October, 2022 that the foregoing resolution was adopted by an affirmative vote of eight (8) in favor - Representatives Chad Counts, Ron Trottier, Sr., Kenneth Malaterre, Elmer Davis, Jr., Lynn Gourneau, Blaine \"Slugger\" Davis, Jon Jon Keplin, Craig Lunday; none (0) opposed; with the Chairman not voting. ___________________________________ Jolean A. Morin, Tribal Secretary ( ) SIGNED INTO LAW/Dated this ___ day of __________, 2022 ( ) VETOED/Dated this ___ day of __________, 2022 ___________________________________ Jamie Azure, Tribal Chairman", "num": "1913-10-22", "path": "library|us/nsn/tmchippewa/council/resolutions|2022|Turtle Mountain Band of Chippewa Indians Res. No. 1913-10-22", "title": "Resolution Number TMBC1913-10-22 of the Duly Elected and Certified Governing Body of the Turtle Mountain Band of Chippewa Indians", "url": "/us/nsn/tmchippewa/council/resolutions/2022/1913-10-22"}
